Let the Level Zero loader find its drivers in the directories listed in
GUIX_LEVEL_ZERO_DRIVER_PATH.

The loader only looks for drivers such as libze_intel_gpu.so.1 in
LD_LIBRARY_PATH and in fixed FHS directories, and loads them by bare
name.  None of these exist on Guix.  With this patch it also searches
GUIX_LEVEL_ZERO_DRIVER_PATH, set by a search path of the package, and
loads a driver found there by its full file name.

--- a/source/loader/linux/driver_discovery_lin.cpp
+++ b/source/loader/linux/driver_discovery_lin.cpp
@@ -108,6 +108,21 @@
   return paths;
 }
 
+// Return the full file name of FILENAME in the first directory of
+// GUIX_LEVEL_ZERO_DRIVER_PATH that has it, or an empty string.
+static std::string findInGuixDriverPath(const std::string& filename) {
+  const char* guixPath = getenv("GUIX_LEVEL_ZERO_DRIVER_PATH");
+  if (guixPath) {
+    for (const auto& dir : splitPaths(guixPath)) {
+      std::string fullPath = dir + "/" + filename;
+      if (fileExistsReadable(fullPath)) {
+        return fullPath;
+      }
+    }
+  }
+  return "";
+}
+
